       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. PB231BITL.
      *> kb/Work PB231 - A BASED RECORD WITH A USAGE BIT LEAF IS
      *> ORDINARY, CELL-BACKED STORAGE. IT RETIRES HALF THE BOUNDARY
      *> conformance:negative/pb164-based-national-leaf PINS, THE SAME
      *> WAY 2023/stepd_based_comp_leaf RETIRED pb151-based-comp-leaf:
      *> THE BIND-TIME COBOLNET1695 WAS REJECTING LEGAL COBOL.
      *> THE DERIVATION IS ONE-DIRECTIONAL AND USES NO ORACLE:
      *>   13.18.5.3 SR1/SR2 - THE ONLY RESTRICTIONS ON THE SUBJECT OF
      *>   A BASED ENTRY ARE "THE SUBJECT OF THE ENTRY SHALL NOT BE OF
      *>   CLASS OBJECT" AND "SHALL NOT BE A DYNAMIC-LENGTH ELEMENTARY
      *>   ITEM OR A VARIABLE-LENGTH GROUP". A GROUP WITH A USAGE BIT
      *>   LEAF IS NEITHER (ITS CLASS IS BOOLEAN, NOT OBJECT), AND NO
      *>   SYNTAX RULE ANYWHERE CONDITIONS BASED ON A SUBORDINATE'S
      *>   USAGE. 14.9.3.3 SR1 - ALLOCATE'S ONLY DEMAND ON data-name-1
      *>   IS "THE DATA ITEM REFERENCED BY data-name-1 SHALL BE
      *>   DESCRIBED WITH THE BASED CLAUSE".
      *> THE BYTE QUANTITY (14.9.3.4 GR3 - "THE NUMBER OF BYTES
      *> REQUIRED TO HOLD AN ITEM AS DESCRIBED BY data-name-1") IS THE
      *> 8.5.1.6.3 CURSOR, NOT A CHARACTER SUM. 13.18.60.4 GR5: "THE
      *> USAGE BIT CLAUSE SPECIFIES THAT BITS SHALL BE USED TO
      *> REPRESENT A BOOLEAN DATA ITEM". 8.5.1.6.3 THEN LAYS R OUT:
      *>   R-B1 PIC 1(4) BIT  -> BYTE 0, BITS 0-3 (THE FIRST BIT
      *>        POSITION OF THE FIRST AVAILABLE BYTE)
      *>   R-B2 PIC 1(4) BIT  -> BYTE 0, BITS 4-7 ("AN ELEMENTARY BIT
      *>        DATA ITEM IMMEDIATELY FOLLOWING AN ELEMENTARY BIT DATA
      *>        ITEM ... OF THE SAME LEVEL" TAKES THE NEXT BIT
      *>        POSITION - THE TWO RUNS SHARE ONE BYTE)
      *>   R-B3 PIC 1(8) BIT  -> BYTE 1, BITS 0-7 (SAME RULE)
      *>   R-X  PIC X(2)      -> BYTES 2-3 ("ALIGNMENT OF ALL OTHER BIT
      *>        DATA ITEMS ... IS AT THE FIRST BIT POSITION OF THE
      *>        FIRST AVAILABLE BYTE" - THE RUN ENDED ON A BYTE EDGE)
      *> SO GR3'S QUANTITY IS 4 BYTES, NOT THE 1+1+1+2 = 5 A CHARACTER
      *> SUM WOULD GIVE. THE WINDOW RB PIC X(4) PROVES IT: A SHORTER
      *> CELL WOULD RAISE EC-BOUND-PTR AT THE DEREFERENCE (13.18.5.4
      *> GR4), AND RB(4:1) READS THE LAST BYTE R OCCUPIES.
      *> GR4a AND GR4b ARE BOTH OBSERVED AND ARE OBSERVED TO BE THE
      *> SAME STORAGE: "a) IF THE RETURNING PHRASE IS SPECIFIED, THE
      *> DATA ITEM REFERENCED BY data-name-2 IS SET TO THE ADDRESS OF
      *> THAT STORAGE, b) IF data-name-1 IS SPECIFIED, THE ADDRESS OF
      *> THE BASED DATA ITEM REFERENCED BY data-name-1 IS SET TO THE
      *> ADDRESS OF THAT STORAGE" - R IS WRITTEN THROUGH ITS OWN
      *> IMPLICIT POINTER AND READ BACK THROUGH WS-P'S WINDOW.
      *> THE BYTES ARE READ WITH FUNCTION ORD, NEVER A SELF-INVERSE
      *> ROUND TRIP (15.70.1: "THE ORDINAL POSITION OF argument-1 IN
      *> THE PROGRAM COLLATING SEQUENCE. THE LOWEST ORDINAL POSITION IS
      *> 1", SO ORD IS THE BYTE VALUE + 1):
      *>   B"0100" | B"0001" = 01000001 = 0x41 =  65 -> ORD  66
      *>   B"01000010"       = 01000010 = 0x42 =  66 -> ORD  67
      *>   "Y"               =            0x59 =  89 -> ORD  90
      *>   "Z"               =            0x5A =  90 -> ORD  91
      *> THE BYTE->BIT DIRECTION THEN PROVES THE CODEC IS AN INVOLUTION
      *> (THE R40 SIGN-LANE LESSON): BYTES WRITTEN THROUGH THE X VIEW
      *> WITH FUNCTION CHAR (15.15.1 - THE INVERSE OF ORD) READ BACK AS
      *> THE BOOLEAN POSITIONS THEY ENCODE - CHAR(256) IS 0xFF, WHOSE
      *> EIGHT BITS SPLIT 1111/1111 ACROSS R-B1/R-B2, AND CHAR(1) IS
      *> 0x00, WHOSE EIGHT BITS ARE R-B3'S 00000000.
      *> GR7 IS EXERCISED ON THE SECOND RECORD: "IF BOTH THE
      *> INITIALIZED PHRASE AND data-name-1 ARE SPECIFIED, THE
      *> ALLOCATED STORAGE IS INITIALIZED AS IF AN INITIALIZE
      *> data-name-1 WITH FILLER ALL TO VALUE THEN TO DEFAULT STATEMENT
      *> WERE EXECUTED". S-B CARRIES A VALUE AND TAKES IT (ALL TO
      *> VALUE); THE FILLER BIT RUN AND S-N DO NOT, SO THEY TAKE
      *> 14.9.20.4 GR6c's DEFAULT SENDING-OPERAND FOR THEIR CATEGORY -
      *> BOOLEAN TAKES "FIGURATIVE CONSTANT ZEROES" (SO 0000, NOT
      *> SPACES), NUMERIC TAKES ZERO - AND WITH FILLER MEANS THE FILLER
      *> RUN IS INCLUDED RATHER THAN SKIPPED.
      *> FREE TAKES THE POINTER, NOT THE RECORD (14.9.15.3 SR1).
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 R BASED.
          05 R-B1 PIC 1(4) USAGE BIT.
          05 R-B2 PIC 1(4) USAGE BIT.
          05 R-B3 PIC 1(8) USAGE BIT.
          05 R-X  PIC X(2).
       01 RB PIC X(4) BASED.
       01 S BASED.
          05 S-B   PIC 1(8) USAGE BIT VALUE B"10110011".
          05 FILLER PIC 1(4) USAGE BIT.
          05 S-N   PIC 9(3).
          05 S-X   PIC X(3) VALUE "HI!".
       01 SB PIC X(8) BASED.
       01 WS-P USAGE POINTER.
       01 WS-Q USAGE POINTER.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
      *> GR4a + GR4b: ONE ALLOCATE, TWO ADDRESSES, ONE STORAGE.
           ALLOCATE R RETURNING WS-P
           SET ADDRESS OF RB TO WS-P
      *> Written through R's own implicit pointer (GR4b) ...
           MOVE B"0100" TO R-B1
           MOVE B"0001" TO R-B2
           MOVE B"01000010" TO R-B3
           MOVE "YZ" TO R-X
           DISPLAY "B1=[" R-B1 "] B2=[" R-B2 "] B3=[" R-B3 "]"
      *> ... and read back through the RETURNING pointer's window (GR4a).
           DISPLAY "ORD=" FUNCTION ORD(RB(1:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(RB(2:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(RB(3:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(RB(4:1))
           DISPLAY "TAIL=[" RB(3:2) "]"
      *> The byte->bit direction (the involution).
           MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(256) TO RB(1:1)
           MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(1) TO RB(2:1)
           DISPLAY "B1=[" R-B1 "] B2=[" R-B2 "] B3=[" R-B3 "]"
           FREE WS-P
      *> GR7 over a record whose leaves include a bit run and a FILLER
      *> bit run: ALL TO VALUE, THEN TO DEFAULT, WITH FILLER.
           ALLOCATE S INITIALIZED RETURNING WS-Q
           SET ADDRESS OF SB TO WS-Q
           DISPLAY "S-B=[" S-B "] S-N=" S-N " S-X=[" S-X "]"
      *> THE FILLER BIT RUN IS UNREFERENCEABLE BY NAME, SO "WITH
      *> FILLER" IS OBSERVED THROUGH THE BYTE WINDOW INSTEAD - BYTE 1
      *> HOLDS ITS FOUR ZERO BITS PLUS THE FOUR IMPLICIT FILLER BITS
      *> 8.5.1.6.3 GENERATES TO ADVANCE S-N TO A BYTE BOUNDARY, SO IT
      *> IS 0x00 AND ITS ORD IS 1. WITHOUT "WITH FILLER" THE RUN WOULD
      *> HAVE BEEN SKIPPED AND THE BYTE LEFT AT THE UNDEFINED FILL.
      *> BYTE 0 IS S-B'S VALUE: B"10110011" = 0xB3 = 179 -> ORD 180.
           DISPLAY "SORD=" FUNCTION ORD(SB(1:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(SB(2:1))
           DISPLAY "SREST=[" SB(3:6) "]"
           FREE WS-Q
           STOP RUN.
